            "text": "Foliage Relief\r\nAbout 1050\r\nKhmer period\r\nAn adoring celestial deity rises from the foliage. This remarkable\r\nbronze must have formed part of a large and very grand\r\ndecorative surround, perhaps flanking a major cult image.\r\nMonumental bronzes are known to have been a feature of\r\nAngkorian Cambodia, and a number are mentioned in a 13thcentury\r\nChinese description of the city.\r\nBronze\r\nCambodia (Angkor)\r\nIn memory of Anthony Gardner. A gift from the beneficiaries of the\r\nAnthony Gardner estate\r\nMuseum no. IS.87-1993",
